  "type": "singleCorrect",
  "level": 3,
  "question": {
    "text": "The pressure $p$, volume $V$ and temperature $T$ for a certain gas are related by $p=\\frac{A T-B T^{2}}{V}$ where $A$ and $B$ are constants. The work done by the gas when the temperature changes from $T_{1}$ to $T_{2}$ while the pressure remains constant, is given by",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "ODnwT",
      "text": "$A\\left(T_{2}-T_{1}\\right)+B\\left(T_{2}^{2}-T_{1}^{2}\\right)$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "W0Xbh",
      "text": "$\\frac{A\\left(T_{2}-T_{1}\\right)}{V_{2}-V_{1}}-\\frac{B\\left(T_{2}^{2}-T_{1}^{2}\\right)}{V_{2}-V_{1}}$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "SQnnt",
      "text": "$ A\\left(\\tau_{2}-T_{1}\\right)-\\frac{B}{2}\\left(T_{2}^{2}-T_{1}^{2}\\right)$",
      "isCorrect": true,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "kyeom",
      "text": "$\\frac{A\\left(T_{2}-T_{1}^{2}\\right)}{V_{2}-V_{1}}$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "Given $P=\\frac{A T-B T^{2}}{V}$\r\n$\\begin{array}{lc}\\Rightarrow & P V=A T-B T^{2} \\\\ \\Rightarrow & P \\Delta V=A \\Delta T-B T \\Delta T\\end{array}$\r\nOn integrating, we get Work $=\\int P d V=A \\int_{T_{1}}^{T_{2}} d T-B \\int_{T_{1}}^{T_{2}} T d T$\r\n$=A\\left(T_{2}-T_{1}\\right)-\\frac{B}{2}\\left[\\left(T_{2}\\right)^{2}-\\left(T_{1}\\right)^{2}\\right]$",
    "image": null
  },
